# oracle: compute xrd on a periodic 4x4x4 fcc Ni crystal (256 atoms, pair_style none, no motion), the BulkNi settings (2Theta 40 80 degrees, c 2 2 2, LP 1): fix ave/time writes the 2theta column c_XRD[1] and the intensity column c_XRD[2] of each reciprocal point (format %.15g, mode vector) at run 0
# oracle: native: b332f28 (installed lmp; compute xrd is in the DIFFRACTION package of that binary)
# oracle-files: w134cp_xrd_ni.txt
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none filerel=1e-8
units           metal
boundary        p p p
lattice         fcc 3.52
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            * 58.71
pair_style      none
compute         XRD all xrd 1.541838 Ni 2Theta 40 80 c 2 2 2 LP 1
fix             1 all ave/time 1 1 1 c_XRD[1] c_XRD[2] mode vector format " %.15g" file w134cp_xrd_ni.txt
thermo_style    custom step pe
run             0
